PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The consensus on the parameters remains firm: the Picard-Fuchs reduction conditions uniquely determine $n_1 = 6$ and $n_2 = 10$, yielding the evaluation point $\alpha = 1/2$ and reducing the system to a standard quadratic-cubic Hamiltonian. Kummer's theorem evaluates the hypergeometric factor at this argument to $\frac{\sqrt{\pi}}{\Gamma(7/12)\Gamma(11/12)}$. While a minority raised the relative-homology convention yielding a factor of $\pi$, the canonical definition of the Hamiltonian period function over closed orbital 1-cycles decisively fixes the prefactor to $2\pi$. The definitive value is $\frac{2\pi^{3/2}}{\Gamma(7/12)\Gamma(11/12)}$.
}

